### Did the U.S. Supreme Court issue any rulings in October or November 2020 concerning the counting of ballots received after Election Day?
Answer: Yes, the U.S. Supreme Court issued a 4-4 decision in October 2020 that allowed a Pennsylvania Supreme Court ruling to stand, permitting Pennsylvania to count ballots received up to three days after Election Day. As the source states, "In a 4-4 decision the U.S. Supreme Court allowed a Pennsylvania Supreme Court decision to stand that requires ballots received up to three days after the election to be counted," with only ballots "clearly postmarked after 8 p.m. on Election Day" excluded from counting if they arrived by 5 p.m. on Nov. 6. Justices Thomas, Alito, Gorsuch, and Kavanaugh voted against allowing the lower court decision to stand.

